# Fixed defect 200, 2026-10-04 (lane b9-recovery; panel 187's cause B3, shape
# `g2/r12`). Symptom: a `function` among a variant's cases was told
# `expected_case` once and dropped with its block, so a mistake inside it,
# `print(1 +)`, waited until it moved out; among a record's fields the same
# function was read as the function it is. Cause: a variant's block was read
# by the case reader alone, which can read no body: the line went with
# `skip_line` and its block with `balanced_block`. A variant's block that
# holds a declaration is read now as a record's is (`records.among_members`,
# `heads.next_member`): a case's line as a case (`member_lines.case_line`), a
# declaration's as the declaration it is, the first told once in the
# variant's words; a word the lexer refused there, `fn`, is the lexer's one
# report. The shapes: a function after a case and before one, a constant, a
# test, a record, a variant, a function with no body, `fn`, and a case's own
# mistake after the function.

variant A
    red
    function f()  #~ expected_case
        print(1 +)  #~ expected_expression

variant B
    function g()  #~ expected_case
        print(1 +)  #~ expected_expression
    red

variant C
    red
    constant K: i64  #~ expected_case
        1 +  #~ expected_expression

variant D
    red
    test "t"  #~ expected_case
        assert 1 +  #~ expected_expression

variant E
    red
    record R  #~ expected_case
        x i64  #~ expected_field_type

variant F
    red
    variant W  #~ expected_case
        a b  #~ expected_end_of_line

variant G
    red
    function h()  #~ expected_case
    #~v missing_body
    blue

variant H
    red
    fn k()  #~ reserved_word
        print(1 +)  #~ expected_expression

variant I
    red
    function m()  #~ expected_case
        print(1 +)  #~ expected_expression
    blue x  #~ expected_end_of_line

function main()
    print(1)
